From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Trall9 <tralllll9@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:49:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] generic: 6.18: fix device_schedule_reprobe for 6.18.64

6.18.64 moved need_parent_lock from struct bus_type to struct
device_type; check dev->type like really_probe() now does.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F55aX2seqR8MdAoMzYRsjG
---
 .../760-04-driver-core-add-device_schedule_reprobe.patch      | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/target/linux/generic/pending-6.18/760-04-driver-core-add-device_schedule_reprobe.patch b/target/linux/generic/pending-6.18/760-04-driver-core-add-device_schedule_reprobe.patch
index baf34a339a7..99641195955 100644
--- a/target/linux/generic/pending-6.18/760-04-driver-core-add-device_schedule_reprobe.patch
+++ b/target/linux/generic/pending-6.18/760-04-driver-core-add-device_schedule_reprobe.patch
@@ -259,8 +259,8 @@ specific to the helper.
 +	 * A bus taking the parent lock would need @dev's parent pinned until
 +	 * the work runs, which device_move() can invalidate.
 +	 */
-+	if (!drv || !dev->bus || dev->bus->need_parent_lock || !dev->p ||
-+	    dev->p->dead || !device_is_registered(dev))
++	if (!drv || !dev->bus || (dev->type && dev->type->need_parent_lock) ||
++	    !dev->p || dev->p->dead || !device_is_registered(dev))
 +		return -EINVAL;
 +
 +	rp = kzalloc_obj(*rp);
